---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import RunFlow from '../components/RunFlow.astro';
import BranchFlow from '../components/BranchFlow.astro';
import AutopilotLog from '../components/AutopilotLog.astro';
import Modes from '../components/Modes.astro';
---
<Base title="How it works · herdr-orchestra" description="One herdr-orchestra run, step by step: plan, edit, build, review the pull request.">
  <section class="first">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h1>One run, from request to pull request.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A run builds one feature. It has 1 to 4 milestones, runs on one feature branch, and ends in a pull request. Here is every step, using a CSV import feature as the example.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="diagram reveal"><RunFlow /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap grid cols-2" style="gap:48px;align-items:start">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Steps 1 to 3</p>
        <h2>You set the goal. The lead writes the plan.</h2>
        <ol class="steps" style="margin-top:28px">
          <li><div><h3>Open your team</h3><p>One pane each: a lead, one or more coders, and an optional reviewer. <code>orch agents launch &lt;kind&gt;</code> prints each agent's command.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><h3>Ask the lead for a feature</h3><p>Run <code>/orch-plan &lt;feature&gt;</code> in the lead's pane. A good request has Feature, Why, Must, Must not, Already decided, Done when.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><h3>The lead researches and plans</h3><p>It reads the codebase, finds the files and patterns involved, and writes milestones as issues. Anything it can't decide goes under Open questions, with options.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><h3>You edit the plan</h3><p><code>.orchestrate/plan.md</code> is a normal Markdown file. Change dependencies, the preferred coder, review yes or no, and answer open questions.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>.orchestrate/plan.md</span></div>
        <pre><span class="t-lead"># Plan: CSV import for transactions</span>
Branch: feature/csv-import
Check command: npm test
Isolation: worktree
Workers: claude-1 (claude), codex-1 (codex)
Reviewer: reviewer (agy)

<span class="t-lead">## [x] M2: Import endpoint</span>
<span class="t-dim">Depends on:</span> M1 (shared ImportRow type)
<span class="t-dim">Prefer:</span> any
<span class="t-dim">Review:</span> yes
<span class="t-dim">Goal:</span> users upload a bank CSV and get rows back
<span class="t-dim">Acceptance criteria:</span>
- POST /imports returns 400 when the
  amount column is missing
<span class="t-dim">Interfaces:</span>
- ImportRow {'{'} date, amount, payee {'}'}
<span class="t-dim">Open questions:</span>
- none
<span class="t-dim">Notes from user:</span>
<span class="t-coder">  Use the existing upload limit (10 MB).</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap grid cols-2" style="gap:48px;align-items:start">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Step 4</p>
        <h2>The team builds, checks and reviews.</h2>
        <ol class="steps" style="margin-top:28px">
          <li><div><h3>Dispatch</h3><p>Each ready milestone goes to a free coder, preferring the kind you asked for. In worktree mode, independent milestones run at once.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><h3>Check</h3><p>When a coder finishes, your check command runs on its work. A failure sends the last 60 lines back, up to 3 rounds.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><h3>Review</h3><p>The reviewer reads the diff and reports blockers. Each blocker round becomes a fix job for the next free coder, up to 2 rounds.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><h3>Land</h3><p>An approved milestone becomes one commit on the feature branch, and the milestones that depended on it unlock.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="diagram-note">The lead can drive this loop (<code>/orch-run</code>), or a script can (<code>orch autopilot</code>). <a href="/docs/driving/">Which to pick →</a></p>
      </div>
      <AutopilotLog />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Step 5</p>
      <h2>One branch, one pull request.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:36px">The run never adds bookkeeping branches or commits to your repo. You get a <code>feature/&lt;name&gt;</code> branch with a real commit per milestone and a summary in <code>.orchestrate/summary.md</code>. Run <code>orch finish</code> and it re-checks the branch, pushes it and opens the pull request.</p>
      <div class="diagram reveal"><BranchFlow /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">When it stops</p>
      <h2>You answer, it resumes.</h2>
      <p class="lede">If a coder asks a question or a round limit is hit, you get a desktop notification that says why. Answer under "Notes from user" in the plan and run <code>orch set Mn pending</code>, or ask the lead to handle it with you. The run picks up where it stopped.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Modes</p>
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:32px">Pick per run.</h2>
      <Modes />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
